---
<section class="why-section not-content">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="hdr">
      <div class="kicker"><span class="bar"></span><span>02 WHY istmo</span></div>
      <h2>Three constraints the framework refuses to break.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <article>
        <div class="num"><span class="d"></span><span>01 EXECUTOR-AGNOSTIC</span></div>
        <h3>Runtime is flume + oneshot + pollster.</h3>
        <p>Call it from tokio, from your own executor, from a blocking thread, from wasm_bindgen_futures. CallHandle is a plain Future. istmo never ships a runtime commitment you did not ask for.</p>
        <span class="chip">zero tokio dep</span>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="num"><span class="d"></span><span>02 GENERATED CLIENTS</span></div>
        <h3>One trait, Rust, Kotlin, Swift.</h3>
        <p>istmo-build parses your crate, derives a Contract, and emits typed dispatchers on both sides. Rename a Rust field; Android and iOS fail to compile next build.</p>
        <span class="chip">build.rs emit()</span>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="num"><span class="d"></span><span>03 ZERO MAGIC</span></div>
        <h3>No inventory. No linkme. No auto-wire.</h3>
        <p>Plugins are declared explicitly in istmo::runtime! &#123; plugins: [EchoClient] &#125;. You can read every frame that crosses the FFI. The wire is wincode, bincode-2 standard.</p>
        <span class="chip">PROTOCOL_VERSION = 4</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
.why-section { padding: 5rem 0; }
.why-section .inner { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2rem; }
.why-section .hdr { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
.why-section .kicker {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem;
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.why-section .kicker .bar { width: 1.5rem; height: 2px; background: #bfff00; }
.why-section h2 {
  font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem);
  line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  margin: 0; color: var(--sl-color-white); font-weight: 700;
  max-width: 55rem;
}
.why-section .grid {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.5rem;
}
@media (max-width: 65rem) {
  .why-section .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
.why-section article {
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  border-radius: 0.75rem; padding: 2rem;
}
.why-section .num {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem;
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.09em; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.why-section .num .d { width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: #bfff00; }
.why-section h3 {
  margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.25;
  letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--sl-color-white); font-weight: 600;
}
.why-section p { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
.why-section .chip {
  display: inline-block; font-family: var(--sl-font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem;
  padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 4px;
  background: var(--sl-color-gray-6); color: var(--sl-color-white);
}
</style>
